.TH OLLAMA-USAGE 1 "September 2026" "ollama-usage 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ollama-usage \- check your Ollama Cloud quota usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ollama-usage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ollama-usage
reads your Ollama Cloud session cookie from a supported local browser and
scrapes
.B https://ollama.com/settings
to report your current session and weekly quota usage, web search / web fetch
request counts, and per-model request statistics.
.PP
Ollama does not yet expose an official quota endpoint, so this tool is a
workaround: it reads your
.B __Secure-session
cookie and scrapes the settings page.  Once an official API ships, this tool
will migrate to it.
.PP
The default output is a human-readable summary.  Additional output modes
.PP
.B plain
(default) \-\- colored multi-line summary with plan name, session and weekly
percentages, reset countdowns, web search / web fetch counts and a
.IR "Models used this week"
list;
.B json
\-\- machine-readable JSON;
.B minidisplay
\-\- one compact line; and
.B minidisplay-horizontal
\-\- the compact view on stacked lines.
.PP
Auto-refresh is enabled by default (every 120 seconds, with a footer showing
the next refresh time).  Use
.B \-\-autorefresh-off
for a single fetch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-minidisplay
Single-line compact output, e.g.:
.sp
.nf
olu (PRO) s: 42.0% (02:46) | w: 77.0% (1d 06:46) ws: 2 wr: 0
.fi
.sp
.RS
.nf
olu = ollama usage, (PRO) = your plan name
s   = session usage,   w = weekly usage (percent used)
ws  = web search requests this session
wr  = web fetch requests this session
.fi
.RE
.sp
Remaining time is shown as [dd] \fIhh:mm\fR (days omitted when zero).  A grey
(mm:ss) countdown is appended and refreshed in place; disable it with
.B \-\-autorefresh-off.
Clears the terminal before showing the line (TTY only).
.TP
.B \-\-minidisplay-horizontal
Multi-line compact output, one item per line:
.sp
.nf
olu (PRO)
s: 42.0% (02:46)
w: 77.0% (1d 06:46)
ws: 2
wr: 0 [auto-refresh-timer]
.fi
.sp
Clears the terminal before showing the output (TTY only) and refreshes the
same way by default.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output the usage as JSON.  The top-level object contains the fields
.IR plan ,
.IR session
(\fIused_pct\fR, \fIresets_at\fR),
.IR weekly
(\fIused_pct\fR, \fIresets_at\fR),
.IR web_search_requests ,
.IR web_fetch_requests
and
.IR models
(a list of \fI{name, requests}\fR objects).  Fields are
.B null
when absent.
.TP
.BI \-\-cookie " COOKIE"
Use a manual
.B __Secure-session
cookie value instead of auto-detection.  Useful when browser detection fails.
.TP
.BI \-\-browser " " { firefox , chrome , edge , brave , opera }
Force a specific browser for cookie auto-detection.
.TP
.B \-\-debug-firefox-profiles
Print every Firefox profile location searched, then exit.  Debugging aid for
cookie auto-detection on macOS/Linux.
.TP
.B \-\-reset-settings
Reset the GUI and widget settings files (see
.B FILES
below) and exit.  Deletes
.B ~/.ollama-usage-gui.cfg
and
.B ~/.ollama-usage-widget.cfg
and restores the defaults on next launch.
.TP
.B \-\-autorefresh-off
Disable continuous refresh (single fetch).  Auto-refresh is on by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-autorefresh " " [ SECONDS ]
Set the refresh interval in SECONDS (default: 120).  Shows a footer with the
next refresh time.  Passed without a value it uses 120.
.TP
.BI \-\-alert " PERCENTAGE"
Exit with code 1 if session, weekly or web search usage exceeds
.IR PERCENTAGE .
Useful for cron jobs and scripts; combine with
.B \-\-quiet
to suppress all output.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress all output; only set the exit code.  Intended for use with
.BR \-\-alert .
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send desktop notifications when session, weekly or web search usage crosses a
threshold.  Requires the
.B notify
extra (py\fIplyer\fR):
.B pip install "ollama-usage[notify]".
Two levels are fired: a
.B warning
at the configured threshold (default 80%) and a
.B critical
notification 15% above it (capped at 100%).  Each level fires once per
threshold crossing \-\- no spam during auto-refresh.
.TP
.BI \-\-notify-threshold " PERCENTAGE"
Threshold for desktop notifications in PERCENTAGE (default: 80).  Requires
.BR \-\-notify .
.TP
.BI \-\-voice-info-when-session-usage-was-reset " [TEXT]"
Speak TEXT aloud when the session usage resets while the CLI is running
(auto-refresh mode).  Default text: "ollama_usage the session usage has been
reset".  Uses the best speech backend found on the system: Kokoro neural TTS
(if kokoro-onnx and the model files are installed), Microsoft Edge-TTS (if
edge-tts is installed), macOS say, Windows PowerShell SAPI, pyttsx3, or the
Linux CLI tools spd-say, espeak-ng, espeak, festival.  Speech runs in a
background thread.  No special hardware is needed - any speakers or
headphones work; the synthesis is pure software.
.TP
.BI \-\-voice-info-when-weekly-usage-was-reset " [TEXT]"
Speak TEXT aloud when the weekly usage resets while the CLI is running
(auto-refresh mode).  Default text: "ollama_usage the weekly usage has been
reset".  Same speech backend requirements as
.BR \-\-voice-info-when-session-usage-was-reset .
.TP
.B \-\-widget
Launch the desktop widget: a small, always-on-top, frameless window showing
live usage gauges.  Auto-refreshes every 30 seconds, is draggable, right-click
opens a context menu (refresh now, toggle size, close), and remembers its
position between runs.  A status indicator in the top-right corner shows the
auto-refresh state: \fBA\fR by default, \fBM\fR with
.BR \-\-autorefresh-off ;
green when the data is fresh, red when an error occurred.  Uses the stdlib
tkinter toolkit (no extra dependency).
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Launch a simple GUI window (OK and Refresh buttons, dark mode toggle, auto-
refresh interval field) showing the same quota information.  Uses tkinter.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " " { dark , light , minimal }
Color scheme used with
.BR \-\-widget .
.TP
.BI \-\-size " " { compact , full }
Widget size: full shows bars plus countdown, compact shows text only.
Restores the last used size when omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-opacity " " 0.0\-1.0
Widget window transparency (default: 0.92; 0.80 with
\-\-background\-transparent).
.TP
.BI \-\-position " " { top\-left , top\-right , bottom\-left , bottom\-right }
Screen corner to place the widget.  Restores the last used position when
omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-background-transparent
Make the widget background fully transparent so only the text and bars are
visible. Native on Windows; on Linux/macOS it requires PySide6 (install
with pip install ollama\-usage[widget]) and otherwise falls back to a
translucent window with a warning.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon ", " \-\-damon
Run the widget, GUI or auto-refresh loop in the background so the terminal can
be closed.  Detaches via fork/setsid and redirects stdio to /dev/null.
.br
Stop with:
.sp
killall ollama_usage            # stops the running instances; the extracted
                                # onefile payload (process name
                                # ollama_usage.bi) shuts down a moment later
pkill -f ollama_usage           # catches every process whose command line matches
.sp
On Windows os.fork is unavailable and \-\-daemon is a no-op.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Stop the CLI (works in every output mode: plain, minidisplay, auto-refresh and
alert loops); prints "Stopped." and exits.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Close the GUI window and the desktop widget.
.SH EXAMPLES
Display current usage (auto-detects the browser):
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage
.fi
.PP
Output as JSON:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --json
.fi
.PP
Force a specific browser:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --browser firefox
.fi
.PP
Pass the cookie manually:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --cookie YOUR_SESSION_COOKIE
.fi
.PP
Alert from a cron job (exit code 1 when usage exceeds 80%, no output):
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --quiet --alert 80
.fi
.PP
Single-line compact view with a 60-second refresh:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --minidisplay --autorefresh 60
.fi
.PP
Notify when usage crosses 75%:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --notify --notify-threshold 75
.fi
.PP
Desktop widget in light theme, compact size, bottom-right:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --widget --theme light --size compact --position bottom-right
.fi
.PP
Widget in the background:
.sp
.nf
ollama-usage --widget --daemon
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the alert threshold was not exceeded.
.TP
.B 1
An alert threshold was exceeded, or an error occurred (authentication
failure, network error, parse error, invalid arguments).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMA_BROWSER_COOKIE
Session cookie used instead of browser auto-detection when set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.ollama-usage-gui.cfg
GUI settings (INI-style): window geometry, dark mode, auto-refresh interval.
.TP
.B ~/.ollama-usage-widget.cfg
Widget settings (INI-style): screen position (\fIx\fR, \fIy\fR) and size
(\fIcompact\fR or \fIfull\fR).
.SH SECURITY
The tool reads your local browser cookie database to authenticate against
ollama.com.  Depending on your operating system and browser, a security prompt
may appear asking permission to access browser cookies or local browser data.
This is expected.
.PP
The cookie grants access to your Ollama account.  Treat it as a secret: do not
paste it into issue reports, logs or chat.
.SH BUGS
This project is not affiliated with Ollama.  It relies on scraping and may
break if ollama.com changes its HTML structure.
.br
Report issues at:
